=begin
  Documentation: https://elanthipedia.play.net/Lich_script_repository#touch

  Empath healing window -- a Lich WebUI take on the Genie "Crutch" plugin.
  It needs a Lich with the WebUI window host; started with --no-gui, Lich
  has no windows to show, and touch says so and stops.

    ;touch            open the window
    ;touch <player>   open the window and TOUCH <player>
    ;touch self       open the window and PERCEIVE HEALTH SELF
    ;touch debug      also log the raw game XML of each TOUCH to touch-debug.log
                      in the Lich log folder (for reporting parsing problems)

  While the window is open, ;touch <player> adds a tab to it instead of
  starting a second copy, and any TOUCH or PERCEIVE HEALTH SELF you type
  yourself is picked up as well.

  Each tab shows the patient's fresh/scar, external/internal wounds on four
  body figures, colored green (minor) through red (useless).

    Left-click a wound      take it -- all of it, or the amount picked under
                            Take > Left-Click Takes (Self tab: cast HW / HS)
    Right-click a wound     Take Part / Half / Most / All
    Vitality bar, P, D      take vitality / poison / disease (Self: VH/FP/CD)
    Right-click a tab       link and take-all options
    Double-click a tab      close it, or every other tab
    Break (right-click)     LINK ALL CANCEL

  Optional settings, for fine-tuning only (the script has its own defaults):
    touch_link_patterns   extra link messages that open a tab, using {name}
    touch_self_spells     per-spell mana (default 5); spells are cast once
                          fully prepared, or after prep_time seconds if set:
                            touch_self_spells:
                              hw:
                                mana: 10
=end

no_pause_all
no_kill_all

arg_definitions = [
  [
    { name: 'target', regex: /^[A-Za-z][\w'-]*$/, optional: true, description: 'Player to TOUCH, SELF to perceive your own health, or DEBUG to log raw TOUCH output' }
  ]
]

args = parse_args(arg_definitions)

# Reads TOUCH / PERCEIVE HEALTH SELF output one plain-text line at a time and
# turns it into events for the patient the output is about. It never touches
# the game or the window, so it can be fed from anywhere.
class TouchParser
  SELF = 'Self'.freeze

  WOUND_TYPES = %i[fresh_external scar_external fresh_internal scar_internal].freeze

  BODY_PARTS = {
    'HEAD'       => :head,
    'RIGHT EYE'  => :right_eye,
    'LEFT EYE'   => :left_eye,
    'NECK'       => :neck,
    'CHEST'      => :chest,
    'ABDOMEN'    => :abdomen,
    'BACK'       => :back,
    'RIGHT ARM'  => :right_arm,
    'LEFT ARM'   => :left_arm,
    'RIGHT HAND' => :right_hand,
    'LEFT HAND'  => :left_hand,
    'RIGHT LEG'  => :right_leg,
    'LEFT LEG'   => :left_leg,
    'SKIN'       => :skin,
    'TAIL'       => :tail
  }.freeze

  # https://elanthipedia.play.net/Damage#Wound_Severity_Levels
  SEVERITIES = {
    'insignificant'               => 1,
    'insignificant to negligible' => 1,
    'negligible'                  => 2,
    'minor'                       => 3,
    'more than minor'             => 4,
    'harmful'                     => 5,
    'very harmful'                => 6,
    'damaging'                    => 7,
    'very damaging'               => 8,
    'severe'                      => 9,
    'very severe'                 => 10,
    'devastating'                 => 11,
    'very devastating'            => 12,
    'useless'                     => 13
  }.freeze

  DEFAULT_LINK_PATTERN = 'You sense a successful empathic link has been forged between you and {name}.'.freeze

  # The severity is the last thing on the line, optionally followed by "(n/13)".
  # Longest names first so "very harmful" is never read as "harmful".
  SEVERITY_PATTERN = Regexp.union(SEVERITIES.keys.sort_by { |key| -key.length })
  WOUND_LINE = %r{^(?<freshness>Fresh|Scars) (?<location>External|Internal):.*?(?<severity>#{SEVERITY_PATTERN})\s*(?:\((?<level>\d+)/13\))?\.?$}
  PART_LINE = /^Wounds to the (?<part>[A-Za-z ]+):/
  INJURIES_SELF = /^Your injuries include/
  INJURIES_OTHER = /^(?<name>[\w'-]+)'s injuries include/
  EMPTINESS = /^You close your eyes, centering your thoughts on your own life essence, but feel only an aching emptiness/
  VITALITY_REMAINING = /\(\S+ ha(?:s|ve) (?<percent>\d+)% vitality remaining\.?\)/
  VITALITY_LOSS = /^(?:\S+ is|You are) .*\((?<percent>\d+)%\)\.$/
  DEAD = /^(?:He|She|They) (?:is|are) dead/
  POISON = /poison(?:ed)?[.!]?$|\bpoisoned\b|^[\w'-]+ (?:has|have) an? .* poison|having trouble breathing/
  DISEASE = /infected|open oozing sores|dormant infection|gangrene|\bdisease\b/
  # How TOUCH output may refer to the patient after naming them.
  PRONOUNS = %w[He She They His Her Their].freeze

  attr_reader :patient

  def self.pattern_to_regex(pattern)
    prefix, suffix = pattern.to_s.split('{name}', 2)
    return nil if suffix.nil?

    /^#{Regexp.escape(prefix.strip)}\s*(?<name>[\w'-]+)#{Regexp.escape(suffix.rstrip)}/
  end

  def initialize(extra_link_patterns = [])
    # touch_link_patterns is optional: nil (an older base.yaml) or junk entries
    # just leave the standard link message.
    patterns = [DEFAULT_LINK_PATTERN] + Array(extra_link_patterns).grep(String)
    @link_regexes = patterns.uniq.filter_map { |pattern| self.class.pattern_to_regex(pattern) }
    @patient = nil
    @parsing = false
    @part = nil
    @poison_count = 0
  end

  def parsing?
    @parsing
  end

  # @param line [String] one line of game text with the XML already stripped
  # @return [Array<Array>] events, each [kind, patient_name, *details]
  def feed(line)
    line = line.to_s.strip
    return [] if line.empty?

    if (name = link_target(line))
      return begin_patient(name)
    elsif INJURIES_SELF.match?(line)
      return begin_patient(SELF)
    elsif EMPTINESS.match?(line)
      events = begin_patient(SELF)
      @parsing = false
      return events
    elsif (match = INJURIES_OTHER.match(line)) && match[:name] == @patient
      @parsing = true
      return []
    end
    return [] unless @parsing
    return finish if line.start_with?('Roundtime')

    parse_detail(line)
  end

  # The game prompt ends a block of TOUCH / PERCEIVE output.
  def finish
    @parsing = false
    @part = nil
    []
  end

  private

  def link_target(line)
    @link_regexes.each do |regex|
      match = regex.match(line)
      return match[:name] if match
    end
    nil
  end

  def begin_patient(name)
    @patient = name
    @parsing = true
    @part = nil
    @poison_count = 0
    [[:patient, name], [:reset, name]]
  end

  def parse_detail(line)
    if (match = PART_LINE.match(line))
      @part = BODY_PARTS[match[:part].strip.upcase]
      []
    elsif (match = WOUND_LINE.match(line))
      wound_event(match)
    elsif (match = VITALITY_REMAINING.match(line))
      [[:vitality, @patient, match[:percent].to_i.clamp(0, 100)]]
    elsif (match = VITALITY_LOSS.match(line))
      [[:vitality, @patient, (100 - match[:percent].to_i).clamp(0, 100)]]
    elsif DEAD.match?(line)
      [[:dead, @patient]]
    else
      condition_events(line)
    end
  end

  def wound_event(match)
    return [] unless @part

    freshness = match[:freshness] == 'Fresh' ? 'fresh' : 'scar'
    type = :"#{freshness}_#{match[:location].downcase}"
    level = match[:level] ? match[:level].to_i : SEVERITIES[match[:severity]]
    [[:wound, @patient, type, @part, level.clamp(1, 13)]]
  end

  def condition_events(line)
    # Only lines about the patient count, as DRCH's poison and disease checks
    # anchor on the subject. Chat or thoughts that land inside a TOUCH burst
    # ([General]-Jim: "im poisoned") start with someone else, so they don't.
    return [] unless about_patient?(line)

    events = []
    if POISON.match?(line)
      @poison_count += 1
      events << [:poison, @patient, @poison_count]
    end
    events << [:disease, @patient] if DISEASE.match?(line)
    events
  end

  # Whether a line is about the patient: it starts with their name (or
  # name's), a pronoun, or for PERCEIVE HEALTH SELF, You or Your. Quoted
  # speech never is: the game's own lines carry no quotation marks, while
  # chat, thoughts and speech always do.
  def about_patient?(line)
    return false if line.include?('"')

    subjects = @patient == SELF ? %w[You Your] : [@patient, "#{@patient}'s", *PRONOUNS]
    first_word = line[/\A[\w'-]+/]
    subjects.include?(first_word)
  end
end

# What we last perceived about one patient.
class TouchPatient
  attr_reader :name, :wounds, :vitality, :poison, :disease, :dead

  def initialize(name)
    @name = name
    reset
  end

  def reset
    @wounds = TouchParser::WOUND_TYPES.to_h { |type| [type, {}] }
    @vitality = 100
    @poison = 0
    @disease = false
    @dead = false
  end

  def apply(event)
    case event.first
    when :reset then reset
    when :wound then @wounds[event[2]][event[3]] = event[4]
    when :vitality then @vitality = event[2]
    when :poison then @poison = event[2]
    when :disease then @disease = true
    when :dead then @dead = true
    end
  end

  def level(type, part)
    @wounds.dig(type, part)
  end

  # @return [Array<Array>] [type, part, level], worst first, ties in perceive order
  def wound_list
    @wounds.flat_map { |type, parts| parts.map { |part, level| [type, part, level] } }
           .each_with_index
           .sort_by { |(_type, _part, level), index| [-level, index] }
           .map(&:first)
  end

  # An independent copy for the window to draw from.
  def snapshot
    {
      wounds: @wounds.transform_values(&:dup),
      vitality: @vitality,
      poison: @poison,
      disease: @disease,
      dead: @dead
    }
  end
end

# Builds the game actions for each healing request. Every method returns a list
# of [:command, text] and [:spell, abbrev, target] actions; nothing is sent here.
class TouchCommands
  SELF = TouchParser::SELF

  SPELL_NAMES = {
    'hw' => 'Heal Wounds', 'hs' => 'Heal Scars', 'vh' => 'Vitality Healing', 'fp' => 'Flush Poisons',
    'cd' => 'Cure Disease', 'heal' => 'Heal', 'regen' => 'Regenerate', 'refresh' => 'Refresh',
    'bs' => 'Blood Staunching', 'foc' => 'Fountain of Creation'
  }.freeze

  # What an action does, in words: the command itself, or e.g.
  # "cast Heal Wounds at left leg external". Tooltips and the status line use
  # this, so they always say exactly what is sent.
  def self.describe(action)
    kind, first, target = action
    return first if kind == :command

    "cast #{SPELL_NAMES.fetch(first, first)}#{" at #{target}" if target}"
  end

  # The task a request starts, for the status strip: who, then what, short
  # enough for the window's default width, e.g. "Pazzlen: Take all" or
  # "Self: Heal left leg (fresh int)". Details are the request's own (wound
  # type and part, condition, link kind, amount, or spell).
  def self.task_label(kind, patient, details = [])
    me = patient == SELF
    what = case kind
           when :touch then me ? 'Perceive health' : 'Touch'
           when :break then 'Break link'
           when :break_all then return 'Cancel all links'
           when :take_wound
             type, part = details
             "#{me ? 'Heal' : 'Take'} #{part_name(part)} (#{type.to_s.sub('ernal', '').tr('_', ' ')})"
           when :take_condition
             condition = details.first
             me ? { 'vitality' => 'Heal vitality', 'poison' => 'Flush poison', 'disease' => 'Cure disease' }[condition] : "Take #{condition}"
           when :take_all then me ? 'Heal all' : 'Take all'
           when :take_minor then me ? 'Heal minor' : 'Take minor'
           when :link then "Link #{details.first}"
           when :link_take then details.first ? "Take #{details.first} of all" : 'Take all'
           when :cast then return "Self: Cast #{SPELL_NAMES.fetch(details.first, details.first)}"
           end
    what && "#{patient}: #{what}"
  end

  # The status strip's text for a step: "Self: Heal all 2/9" while it runs,
  # "Pazzlen: Take vitality - done" once its task has been sent, and
  # "Self: Heal all - stopped at 3/9" after Break or Stop. "done" means
  # sent, not that the game agreed.
  def self.status_text(step, state)
    label = step[:label] || TouchCommands.describe(step[:action])
    progress = "#{step[:step]}/#{step[:steps]}" if step[:steps] > 1
    case state
    when :running then [label, progress].compact.join(' ')
    when :done then "#{label} - done"
    else "#{label} - stopped#{" at #{progress}" if progress}"
    end
  end

  def self.part_name(part)
    part.to_s.tr('_', ' ')
  end

  def self.internal?(type)
    type.to_s.end_with?('internal')
  end

  def self.scar?(type)
    type.to_s.start_with?('scar')
  end

  def self.scar_of(type)
    internal?(type) ? :scar_internal : :scar_external
  end

  def self.touch(patient)
    return [[:command, 'perceive health self']] if patient == SELF

    [[:command, "touch #{patient}"]]
  end

  # On Self, Heal Wounds / Heal Scars are cast at the area, naming the layer
  # that was clicked (CAST <area> INTERNAL or EXTERNAL). A plain CAST <area>
  # would spend its healing on external wounds first.
  #
  # @param method [String, nil] 'part', 'half' or 'most'; nil or 'all' takes it all
  def self.take_wound(patient, type, part, method = nil, quick: false)
    if patient == SELF
      layer = internal?(type) ? 'internal' : 'external'
      return [[:spell, scar?(type) ? 'hs' : 'hw', "#{part_name(part)} #{layer}"]]
    end

    # In the game's own order: TAKE <patient> <area> [PART|HALF|MOST] [QUICK]
    # [INTERNAL] [SCAR] (from typing TAKE with no arguments).
    words = ['take', patient, part_name(part)]
    words << method if method && method != 'all'
    words << 'quick' if quick
    words << 'internal' if internal?(type)
    words << 'scar' if scar?(type)
    [[:command, words.join(' ')]]
  end

  # Taking a whole wound: half of anything very damaging (8/13) or worse when
  # Half On Major is set, as Genie Crutch did, otherwise all of it.
  def self.take_full(patient, type, part, level, options)
    method = 'half' if options[:half_on_major] && level > 7
    take_wound(patient, type, part, method, quick: options[:quick])
  end

  # A left-click takes the amount picked under Take > Left-Click Takes. All,
  # the default, is a whole take, so it follows Half On Major.
  def self.click_wound(patient, type, part, level, options)
    amount = options[:click_amount].to_s
    return take_full(patient, type, part, level, options) unless %w[part half most].include?(amount)

    take_wound(patient, type, part, amount, quick: options[:quick])
  end

  def self.take_condition(patient, condition, options)
    if patient == SELF
      spell = { 'vitality' => 'vh', 'poison' => 'fp', 'disease' => 'cd' }.fetch(condition)
      return [[:spell, spell, nil]]
    end

    quick = ' quick' if options[:quick]
    return [[:command, "take #{patient} vitality#{quick}"]] if condition == 'vitality'

    [[:command, "take #{patient}#{quick} #{condition}"]]
  end

  # Every wound the options allow, worst first, then the scars those leave
  # behind, then a fresh TOUCH so the tab redraws. Uses the game's own
  # TAKE EVERYTHING when no option needs wound-by-wound control; that path also
  # touches first, as Genie Crutch did, so the link is fresh for the TAKE.
  def self.take_all(patient, wounds, options)
    if patient != SELF && bulk_take?(options)
      return touch(patient) + [[:command, "take #{patient} everything#{' quick' if options[:quick]}"]] + touch(patient)
    end

    taken = wounds.reject { |type, _part, level| skip?(type, level, options) }
    actions = taken.flat_map { |type, part, level| take_full(patient, type, part, level, options) }
    if options[:include_scars] && patient != SELF
      taken.reject { |type, _part, _level| scar?(type) }.each do |type, part, level|
        actions.concat(take_full(patient, scar_of(type), part, level, options))
      end
    end
    actions.concat(touch(patient)) unless patient == SELF
    actions.uniq
  end

  # Only the wounds below harmful. A patient is touched before (a fresh link)
  # and after (so the tab redraws).
  def self.take_minor(patient, wounds, options)
    minor = wounds.select { |type, _part, level| level < 5 && !filtered?(type, options) }
    takes = minor.flat_map { |type, part, _level| take_wound(patient, type, part, quick: options[:quick]) }.uniq
    return takes if patient == SELF

    touch(patient) + takes + touch(patient)
  end

  def self.link(patient, kind)
    links = { 'persistent' => %w[persistent], 'hodierna' => %w[persistent hodierna], 'unity' => %w[unity] }.fetch(kind)
    touch(patient) + links.map { |link| [:command, "link #{patient} #{link}"] }
  end

  # TAKE <patient> EVERYTHING [PART|HALF|MOST] [QUICK]: every wound and scar.
  #
  # @param method [String, nil] 'part', 'half', 'most', or nil for all of it
  def self.link_take(patient, method, options)
    words = ['take', patient, 'everything']
    words << method if method
    words << 'quick' if options[:quick]
    touch(patient) + [[:command, words.join(' ')]] + touch(patient)
  end

  def self.break_link(patient)
    return [] if patient.nil? || patient == SELF

    [[:command, "break #{patient}"]]
  end

  def self.bulk_take?(options)
    !options[:leave_bleeders] && !options[:half_on_major] && options[:include_internal] && options[:include_scars]
  end

  def self.filtered?(type, options)
    (!options[:include_internal] && internal?(type)) || (!options[:include_scars] && scar?(type))
  end

  # Leaving bleeders means skipping fresh wounds past harmful.
  def self.skip?(type, level, options)
    return true if filtered?(type, options)

    options[:leave_bleeders] && level > 5 && !scar?(type)
  end
end

# The window, drawn by Lich's WebUI. Its callbacks run on a WebUI host
# thread, where there is no script context: they only record what was asked
# and push intents onto the queue passed in. The script's own thread does all
# game I/O and answers with show_patient / update_patient / show_activity.
class TouchWindow
  # Tabs and figures are drawn on Genie Crutch's own grids and scaled to fit:
  # a tab is at least 165x322, a body figure 63x134.
  TAB_WIDTH = 165.0
  # Genie's 322, plus room under the bottom captions so they are never clipped.
  TAB_HEIGHT = 326.0
  FIGURE_WIDTH = 63.0

  # [x, y, width, height, shape, caption] on the figure grid, in drawing order.
  FIGURE_PARTS = {
    head: [12, 2, 34, 34, :round, nil],
    right_eye: [16, 11, 12, 12, :round, nil],
    left_eye: [30, 11, 12, 12, :round, nil],
    neck: [22, 35, 14, 9, :square, nil],
    chest: [13, 43, 32, 23, :square, nil],
    back: [13, 65, 32, 16, :square, 'back'],
    abdomen: [13, 80, 32, 16, :square, nil],
    right_arm: [2, 43, 12, 35, :square, nil],
    left_arm: [44, 43, 12, 35, :square, nil],
    right_hand: [2, 77, 12, 12, :round, nil],
    left_hand: [44, 77, 12, 12, :round, nil],
    right_leg: [13, 95, 13, 37, :square, nil],
    left_leg: [32, 95, 13, 37, :square, nil],
    tail: [6, 93, 8, 20, :square, nil],
    skin: [47, 91, 15, 17, :round, 'S']
  }.freeze

  # [column, y, caption] of each figure on the tab grid.
  FIGURES = {
    fresh_external: [:left, 25, 'Fresh External'],
    scar_external: [:right, 25, 'Scar External'],
    fresh_internal: [:left, 175, 'Fresh Internal'],
    scar_internal: [:right, 175, 'Scar Internal']
  }.freeze

  # Wound level 0 (none) through 11+, green to red, as 0-255 RGB.
  LEVEL_COLORS = [
    [0, 0, 0], [0, 94, 32], [46, 121, 26], [98, 151, 20], [152, 182, 13], [206, 213, 6],
    [255, 242, 0], [255, 204, 0], [255, 153, 0], [255, 102, 0], [255, 51, 0], [255, 0, 0]
  ].freeze
  # Shown for a moment on whatever was clicked, so a click visibly registers.
  PRESSED_COLOR = [32, 178, 150].freeze
  ALERT_COLOR = [255, 0, 0].freeze
  WHITE = [255, 255, 255].freeze
  EDGE_COLOR = [128, 128, 128].freeze
  # Wound level => severity name, for tooltips (1 is plain "insignificant").
  SEVERITY_NAMES = TouchParser::SEVERITIES.each_with_object({}) { |(severity, level), names| names[level] ||= severity }.freeze

  # More > Cast On Self, in menu order.
  SPELLS = %w[heal regen refresh bs foc vh fp cd].map { |abbrev| [TouchCommands::SPELL_NAMES[abbrev], abbrev] }.freeze
  # Take menu check items, in order; nil is a separator.
  TAKE_OPTIONS = [
    ['Including Internal', :include_internal], ['Including Scars', :include_scars], nil,
    ['Quick', :quick], ['Half On Major', :half_on_major], ['Leave Bleeders', :leave_bleeders]
  ].freeze
  # Take > Left-Click Takes.
  CLICK_AMOUNTS = [%w[Part part], %w[Half half], %w[Most most], %w[All all]].freeze
  WOUND_METHODS = [['Take Part', 'part'], ['Take Half', 'half'], ['Take Most', 'most'], ['Take All', 'all']].freeze

  PAGE_ID = 'touch'.freeze
  DEFAULT_WIDTH = 420
  DEFAULT_HEIGHT = 640
  # The toolbar needs this much width; a smaller saved size (such as one the
  # GTK window left behind) is raised to it.
  MIN_WIDTH = 400
  MIN_HEIGHT = 420
  # Window space the toolbar, tab headers and status strip take from the figures.
  CHROME_WIDTH = 20
  CHROME_HEIGHT = 112
  PANEL_PADDING = 16
  # Composite pixels per grid unit, so half units stay exact; the composite's
  # own scale does the zooming.
  UNIT = 2
  # The thickest ring the composite draws; a larger round part is filled with
  # rings inside one another.
  MAX_RING = 16
  # How long a clicked target is drawn pressed, in milliseconds.
  FLASH_MS = 150
  # The status strip when nothing is queued or being cast.
  READY = 'Ready'.freeze

  # Whether this Lich can show native WebUI windows. Without it (an older
  # Lich, or one started with --no-gui) the script says so and stops.
  def self.available?
    defined?(Lich::WebUI) && Lich::WebUI.respond_to?(:presentation_enabled?) && Lich::WebUI.presentation_enabled? &&
      defined?(Lich::API) && Lich::API.respond_to?(:webui_page) ? true : false
  end

  # A component key for a patient: names may hold an apostrophe, which keys
  # cannot.
  def self.key_for(name)
    name.to_s.gsub(/[^A-Za-z0-9_.:-]/) { |char| format('_%02x', char.ord) }
  end

  # Where everything sits on the tab grid for a drawing area of the given
  # size in pixels. One scale for both axes keeps the figures in proportion;
  # any width beyond the 165-unit grid widens the vitality bar and spreads
  # the two figure columns out. At exactly 165 wide this is Genie Crutch's
  # own layout.
  #
  # @return [Hash] :scale (pixels per grid unit), :width (grid units), the
  #   :vitality, :close, :poison and :disease boxes, and :figures
  #   (type => [x, y, caption])
  def self.tab_layout(width_px, height_px)
    scale = [width_px / TAB_WIDTH, height_px / TAB_HEIGHT].min.clamp(0.5, 6.0)
    width = [width_px / scale, TAB_WIDTH].max
    columns = { left: width / 4.0 - FIGURE_WIDTH / 2.0, right: width * 3 / 4.0 - FIGURE_WIDTH / 2.0 }
    {
      scale: scale,
      width: width,
      vitality: [5, 5, width - 30, 17],
      close: [width - 21, 5, 17, 17],
      poison: [width / 2.0 - 8, 27, 16, 17],
      disease: [width / 2.0 - 8, 50, 16, 17],
      figures: FIGURES.transform_values { |column, y, caption| [columns[column], y, caption] }
    }
  end

  # @return [Array, nil] [:close], [:vitality], [:poison], [:disease] or
  #   [:part, type, part] for a region key
  def self.target_for(region)
    kind, first, second = region.to_s.split('.')
    if kind == 'b' && %w[close vitality poison disease].include?(first)
      [first.to_sym]
    elsif kind == 'w' && TouchParser::WOUND_TYPES.include?(first&.to_sym) && FIGURE_PARTS.key?(second&.to_sym)
      [:part, first.to_sym, second.to_sym]
    end
  end

  def self.region_key(target)
    target.first == :part ? "w.#{target[1]}.#{target[2]}" : "b.#{target.first}"
  end

  # Hover text: what the target is and what a click does. The click lines are
  # built from the very actions a click queues, so they always match what is
  # sent.
  def self.tooltip_for(name, target, snapshot, options)
    case target.first
    when :close then 'Close this tab'
    when :vitality then click_hint(TouchCommands.take_condition(name, 'vitality', options))
    when :poison
      state = snapshot[:poison].to_i.positive? ? "Poisoned (#{snapshot[:poison]})" : 'No poison perceived'
      "#{state}\n#{click_hint(TouchCommands.take_condition(name, 'poison', options))}"
    when :disease
      state = snapshot[:disease] ? 'Diseased' : 'No disease perceived'
      "#{state}\n#{click_hint(TouchCommands.take_condition(name, 'disease', options))}"
    when :part then wound_tooltip(name, snapshot, target[1], target[2], options)
    end
  end

  def self.wound_tooltip(name, snapshot, type, part, options)
    level = snapshot.dig(:wounds, type, part)
    heading = "#{type.to_s.split('_').map(&:capitalize).join(' ')} #{TouchCommands.part_name(part)}"
    return "#{heading}: no wound" unless level

    hint = click_hint(TouchCommands.click_wound(name, type, part, level, options))
    hint += "\nRight-click: take part, half or most" unless name == TouchParser::SELF
    "#{heading}: #{SEVERITY_NAMES[level]} (#{level}/13)\n#{hint}"
  end

  def self.click_hint(actions)
    "Click: #{actions.map { |action| TouchCommands.describe(action) }.join(', then ')}"
  end

  def self.vitality_color(percent)
    return LEVEL_COLORS[1] if percent >= 100

    LEVEL_COLORS[(11 - (percent - 1).div(10)).clamp(2, 11)]
  end

  # Black or white, whichever reads better on the fill color.
  def self.text_color_on(rgb)
    red, green, blue = rgb.map { |channel| channel / 255.0 }
    (0.299 * red) + (0.587 * green) + (0.114 * blue) > 0.55 ? [0, 0, 0] : WHITE
  end

  def self.rgba(rgb, alpha = 1.0)
    { r: rgb[0], g: rgb[1], b: rgb[2], a: alpha }
  end

  # Grid units to composite pixels.
  def self.px(value)
    (value * UNIT).round
  end

  # Every layer of one patient's tab: the vitality bar, close box, P and D
  # markers, the four body figures, then one clickable region per target,
  # which carries the target's tooltip.
  #
  # @param pressed [Array, nil] the target drawn pressed, if any
  # @return [Array<Hash>] composite layers, in grid units times UNIT
  def self.tab_layers(name, snapshot, layout, options, pressed = nil)
    pressed_kind = pressed&.first
    layers = vitality_layers(layout[:vitality], snapshot, pressed_kind == :vitality)
    layers.concat(close_layers(layout[:close], pressed_kind == :close))
    layers.concat(marker_layers(layout[:poison], 'P', snapshot[:poison].positive?, pressed_kind == :poison))
    layers.concat(marker_layers(layout[:disease], 'D', snapshot[:disease], pressed_kind == :disease))
    if snapshot[:poison] > 1
      poison_x, poison_y, poison_width, = layout[:poison]
      layers << label(poison_x + poison_width + 1, poison_y + 2, 10, 13, snapshot[:poison].to_s, 10)
    end
    layout[:figures].each do |type, (figure_x, figure_y, caption)|
      layers.concat(figure_layers(snapshot[:wounds][type], type, figure_x, figure_y, pressed))
      layers << label(figure_x - 9, figure_y + 135, 82, 12, caption, 10.5)
    end
    layers.concat(region_layers(name, snapshot, layout, options))
  end

  def self.vitality_layers(box, snapshot, pressed)
    x, y, width, height = box
    percent = snapshot[:vitality]
    color = vitality_color(percent)
    text = snapshot[:dead] ? "DEAD #{percent}%" : "Vitality #{percent}%"
    # The label spans the colored and the black part of the bar; it takes
    # the color that reads on whichever is under its middle.
    under = percent >= 50 ? color : LEVEL_COLORS[0]
    [
      rect(x, y, width, height, LEVEL_COLORS[0]),
      rect(x, y, width * percent / 100.0, height, color),
      rect(x, y, width, height, pressed ? PRESSED_COLOR : EDGE_COLOR, mode: 'stroke', line: pressed ? 3 : 1.5),
      label(x, y, width, height, text, 11, color: text_color_on(under))
    ]
  end

  def self.close_layers(box, pressed)
    x, y, width, height = box
    layers = []
    layers << rect(x, y, width, height, PRESSED_COLOR) if pressed
    layers << rect(x, y, width, height, EDGE_COLOR, mode: 'stroke', line: 1.5)
    layers << label(x, y, width, height, 'x', 13)
  end

  def self.marker_layers(box, letter, active, pressed)
    x, y, width, height = box
    fill = active ? ALERT_COLOR : LEVEL_COLORS[0]
    disc(x, y, width, height, fill) +
      [ring(x, y, width, height, pressed ? PRESSED_COLOR : WHITE, pressed ? 3 : 1.5),
       label(x, y, width, height, letter, 10, color: text_color_on(fill))]
  end

  def self.figure_layers(levels, type, figure_x, figure_y, pressed)
    layers = []
    FIGURE_PARTS.each do |part, (x, y, width, height, shape, caption)|
      next if part == :tail && !levels[:tail]

      fill = part_color(levels, type, part, pressed)
      left = figure_x + x
      top = figure_y + y
      if shape == :square
        layers << rect(left, top, width, height, fill)
        layers << rect(left, top, width, height, WHITE, mode: 'stroke', line: 1.5)
      else
        layers.concat(disc(left, top, width, height, fill))
        layers << ring(left, top, width, height, WHITE, 1.5)
      end
      layers << label(left, top, width, height, caption, height * 0.6, color: text_color_on(fill)) if caption
    end
    layers << label(figure_x, figure_y + 26, 8, 12, 'R', 9.5)
    layers << label(figure_x + 55, figure_y + 26, 8, 12, 'L', 9.5)
  end

  def self.part_color(levels, type, part, pressed)
    return PRESSED_COLOR if targets_part?(pressed, levels, type, part)

    level = levels[part] || (%i[left_eye right_eye].include?(part) ? levels[:head] : nil) || 0
    LEVEL_COLORS[level.clamp(0, 11)]
  end

  # Whether a pressed target lights this part. An unhurt eye is drawn in the
  # head's color, so it lights with the head too.
  def self.targets_part?(target, levels, type, part)
    return false unless target&.first == :part && target[1] == type
    return true if target[2] == part

    %i[left_eye right_eye].include?(part) && target[2] == :head && !levels[part]
  end

  # One region per part (in drawing order, so an eye sits over the head),
  # then the boxes. Every part has one, hurt or not, as the old window's hit
  # test did: a click on an unhurt part says there is nothing to take.
  def self.region_layers(name, snapshot, layout, options)
    regions = []
    layout[:figures].each do |type, (figure_x, figure_y, _caption)|
      levels = snapshot[:wounds][type]
      FIGURE_PARTS.each do |part, (x, y, width, height, _shape, _caption)|
        next if part == :tail && !levels[:tail]

        regions << region([:part, type, part], figure_x + x, figure_y + y, width, height, name, snapshot, options)
      end
    end
    %i[vitality poison disease close].each do |box|
      regions << region([box], *layout[box], name, snapshot, options)
    end
    regions
  end

  def self.region(target, x, y, width, height, name, snapshot, options)
    { kind: 'region', key: region_key(target), x1: px(x), y1: px(y), x2: px(x + width), y2: px(y + height),
      label: tooltip_for(name, target, snapshot, options), activates: true }
  end

  def self.rect(x, y, width, height, color, mode: 'fill', line: nil)
    layer = { kind: 'rectangle', mode: mode, x: x * UNIT, y: y * UNIT, w: [width * UNIT, 0].max, h: [height * UNIT, 0].max, color: rgba(color) }
    layer[:line_width] = line if line
    layer
  end

  def self.ring(x, y, width, height, color, line)
    { kind: 'marker', shape: 'ring', x: px(x), y: px(y), w: px(width), h: px(height), color: rgba(color), line_width: line }
  end

  # A filled circle or ellipse: rings no thicker than MAX_RING, each inside
  # the last, until nothing is left in the middle.
  def self.disc(x, y, width, height, color)
    left = px(x)
    top = px(y)
    width = px(width)
    height = px(height)
    layers = []
    while width.positive? && height.positive?
      half = [width, height].min / 2.0
      line = [half, MAX_RING].min
      layers << { kind: 'marker', shape: 'ring', x: left, y: top, w: width, h: height, color: rgba(color), line_width: [line, 1].max }
      break if half <= MAX_RING

      left += MAX_RING
      top += MAX_RING
      width -= 2 * MAX_RING
      height -= 2 * MAX_RING
    end
    layers
  end

  def self.label(x, y, width, height, text, size, color: nil)
    layer = { kind: 'label', x: px(x), y: px(y), w: px(width), h: px(height), text: text, align: 'center',
              emphasis: 'strong', font_size: (size * UNIT).round(1), font_unit: 'px' }
    color ? layer.merge(foreground: rgba(color)) : layer
  end

  # Whether a reported window position is worth saving: a minimized window
  # reports a position far off-screen (about -32000 on Windows), which would
  # reopen it where it cannot be seen. When the host names its screens, the
  # title bar must be on one of them.
  def self.on_screen?(x, y, monitors = nil)
    return false unless x.is_a?(Integer) && y.is_a?(Integer)
    return false if x < -10_000 || y < -10_000

    screens = monitors.is_a?(Hash) ? Array(monitors[:screens]) : []
    return true if screens.empty?

    screens.any? do |screen|
      (x + 40).between?(screen[:x], screen[:x] + screen[:width]) && (y + 10).between?(screen[:y], screen[:y] + screen[:height])
    end
  end

  # Window position, size, pin and the Take menu toggles, for the script to
  # save on exit. Replaced (never mutated) so another thread can read it.
  attr_reader :state

  # Registers the page and opens the window.
  #
  # @param owner [Object] the running Script, which owns the page
  # @param intents [Thread::Queue] where requests go for the script thread
  # @param state [Hash] the saved window state (see #state)
  # @raise [RuntimeError] if the window could not be opened
  def initialize(owner, intents, state)
    @owner = owner
    @intents = intents
    @state = state
    @options = state['options'].transform_keys(&:to_sym)
    @lock = Monitor.new
    @views = {}
    @selected = nil
    @tabs_revision = 0
    @menu_revision = 0
    @tab_menu = nil
    @right_target = nil
    @activity = { text: READY, detail: nil, state: :done }
    @size = [[(state['width'] || DEFAULT_WIDTH).to_i, MIN_WIDTH].max, [(state['height'] || DEFAULT_HEIGHT).to_i, MIN_HEIGHT].max]
    @resize_id = 0
    @closed = false
    open_page
  end

  def show_patient(name, snapshot)
    @lock.synchronize do
      unless @views[name]
        @views[name] = { snapshot: nil, pressed: nil }
      end
      @views[name][:snapshot] = snapshot
      select_tab(name)
    end
    retitle
    refresh
  end

  def update_patient(name, snapshot)
    @lock.synchronize do
      return unless @views[name]

      @views[name][:snapshot] = snapshot
    end
    refresh
  end

  # Updates the status strip: a busy bar and a Stop button while running; the
  # text dimmed once done or stopped, where it stays as the last thing Touch
  # did.
  #
  # @param detail [String] the exact command or cast, for the tooltip
  # @param state [Symbol] :running, :done or :stopped
  def show_activity(text, detail, state)
    @lock.synchronize { @activity = { text: text, detail: detail, state: state } }
    refresh
  end

  # Brings the window forward (;touch with no name while it is open).
  def present
    Lich::API.webui_open(page: @page) unless @closed
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  # Closes the window. The WebUI service is shared with other scripts, so the
  # owner's pages are retired, never the service stopped.
  def destroy
    @closed = true
    Lich::WebUI.terminate_owner(@owner)
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  def selected_patient
    @lock.synchronize { @selected if @views.key?(@selected) }
  end

  # Renders the page now. A refresh after the window has gone is ignored.
  def refresh
    Lich::API.webui_refresh(@page) if @page && !@closed
  rescue Lich::WebUI::Error
    nil
  end

  # Wraps a WebUI callback: an error is reported rather than lost on the host
  # thread, and the page is redrawn afterwards unless redraw is false (a
  # redraw between a press and its click would swallow the click).
  def cb(redraw: true, &block)
    window = self
    lambda do |event|
      block.call(event)
    rescue StandardError => e
      Lich::Messaging.msg('bold', "touch: window error: #{e.class}: #{e.message}")
    ensure
      window.refresh if redraw
    end
  end

  # ---- page --------------------------------------------------------------

  # Everything the page shows, read under the lock in one go so a render
  # never sees half an update.
  def model
    @lock.synchronize do
      area = [@size[0] - CHROME_WIDTH, @size[1] - CHROME_HEIGHT]
      # Less the tab page's own padding, so the figures need no scrollbar.
      layout = self.class.tab_layout(area[0] - PANEL_PADDING, area[1] - PANEL_PADDING)
      tabs = @views.map do |name, view|
        snapshot = view[:snapshot]
        { name: name, key: self.class.key_for(name),
          layers: snapshot ? self.class.tab_layers(name, snapshot, layout, @options, view[:pressed]) : [] }
      end
      {
        layout: layout, area: area, tabs: tabs, selected: tabs.index { |tab| tab[:name] == @selected } || 0,
        tabs_revision: @tabs_revision, menu_revision: @menu_revision, tab_menu: @tab_menu,
        activity: @activity, options: @options.dup, pinned: @state['pinned'] ? true : false
      }
    end
  end

  # Builds the page. Component blocks run with the builder as self, so
  # everything inside them goes through the locals ui, window and data.
  def render(ui)
    window = self
    data = model
    ui.facility(:presentation, { always_on_top: data[:pinned] })
    ui.stack(key: 'body', gap: 2, fill: true) do
      window.render_toolbar(ui, data)
      if data[:tabs].empty?
        ui.text(key: 'hint', emphasis: 'subtle', align: 'center', margin: 12, line_justify: :center,
                content: "No patients yet\n\nTOUCH someone, or ;touch <name>.\nPERCEIVE HEALTH SELF opens your own tab.")
      else
        window.render_tabs(ui, data)
      end
      window.render_status(ui, data[:activity])
    end
    render_wound_menu(ui)
    render_tab_menu(ui, data)
  end

  def render_toolbar(ui, data)
    window = self
    ui.stack(key: 'toolbar', orientation: 'horizontal', gap: 2) do
      ui.button(key: 'touch', label: 'Touch',
                tooltip: 'Touch the patient on this tab again. To add a patient: TOUCH <name> or ;touch <name>.',
                on: { activate: window.cb { window.on_touch } })
      ui.button(key: 'break', label: 'Break', pointer_events: true,
                tooltip: "Stop: cancel what is queued or being cast, and break the link to this patient.\nRight-click: stop and LINK ALL CANCEL",
                on: { activate: window.cb { window.on_break },
                      pointer_press: window.cb(redraw: false) { |event| window.on_break_press(event.payload) } })
      ui.group(key: 'take', label: 'Take', menu: :popover, tooltip: 'Take Minor / Take All, and what they include') do
        ui.button(key: 'take-minor', label: 'Take Minor', on: { activate: window.cb { window.send_for_selected(:take_minor) } })
        ui.button(key: 'take-all', label: 'Take All', on: { activate: window.cb { window.send_for_selected(:take_all) } })
        ui.divider(key: 'take-sep-0')
        TAKE_OPTIONS.each_with_index do |(label, option), index|
          next ui.divider(key: "take-sep-#{index + 1}") unless label

          ui.toggle(key: "opt-#{option}", label: label, appearance: :menu, checked: data[:options][option] ? true : false,
                    on: { change: window.cb { |event| window.set_option(option, event.payload[:value]) } })
        end
        # Sections rather than nested submenus: a redraw while a take runs
        # reopens the dropdown but would close a submenu inside it.
        ui.divider(key: 'take-sep-amounts', label: 'Left-Click Takes')
        CLICK_AMOUNTS.each do |label, amount|
          ui.radio_option(key: "amount-#{amount}", label: label, appearance: :menu, group: 'click-amount',
                          checked: data[:options][:click_amount] == amount,
                          on: { change: window.cb { |event| window.set_click_amount(amount) if event.payload[:value] } })
        end
      end
      ui.button(key: 'all', label: 'All', tooltip: 'Take everything the Take menu options allow',
                on: { activate: window.cb { window.send_for_selected(:take_all) } })
      ui.group(key: 'more', label: 'More', menu: :popover, tooltip: 'Perceive yourself, cast on yourself, reset the size') do
        ui.button(key: 'perceive-self', label: 'Perceive Health Self',
                  on: { activate: window.cb { window.push([:touch, TouchParser::SELF]) } })
        ui.divider(key: 'more-sep-0', label: 'Cast On Self')
        SPELLS.each do |label, abbrev|
          ui.button(key: "cast-#{abbrev}", label: label, on: { activate: window.cb { window.push([:cast, nil, abbrev]) } })
        end
        ui.divider(key: 'more-sep-1')
        ui.button(key: 'reset-size', label: 'Reset Size', on: { activate: window.cb { window.reset_size } })
      end
      ui.toggle(key: 'pin', label: 'Pin', appearance: :button, checked: data[:pinned],
                tooltip: 'Keep this window in front of every other window',
                on: { change: window.cb { |event| window.set_pinned(event.payload[:value]) } })
    end
  end

  def render_tabs(ui, data)
    window = self
    layout = data[:layout]
    tabs = data[:tabs]
    ui.tabs(key: "patients-#{data[:tabs_revision]}", names: tabs.map { |tab| tab[:name] }, selected: data[:selected],
            headers: tabs.map { |tab| { key: tab[:key], pointer_events: true } },
            on: { select: window.cb { |event| window.on_select(event.payload) },
                  tab_pointer: window.cb(redraw: false) { |event| window.on_tab_pointer(event.payload) } }) do
      tabs.each do |tab|
        name = tab[:name]
        menu = name == TouchParser::SELF ? {} : { context_menu: 'wound-menu' }
        # A scroller around the figures: a tab page itself would squeeze them.
        ui.scroll(slot: name, key: "view-#{tab[:key]}", height: data[:area][1]) do
          ui.composite(key: "figure-#{tab[:key]}", width: TouchWindow.px(layout[:width]), height: TouchWindow.px(TAB_HEIGHT),
                       scale: (layout[:scale] / UNIT).clamp(0.1, 8.0), surface_events: true, layers: tab[:layers], **menu,
                       on: { region_activate: window.cb { |event| window.on_region(name, event.payload[:region]) },
                             surface_activate: window.cb(redraw: false) { |event| window.on_surface(name, event.payload) } })
        end
      end
    end
  end

  def render_status(ui, activity)
    window = self
    running = activity[:state] == :running
    tooltip = running ? "#{activity[:text]}\nNow: #{activity[:detail]}" : activity[:text]
    ui.stack(key: 'status', orientation: 'horizontal', gap: 6, margin: { left: 6, right: 4 }) do
      ui.progress(key: 'busy', indeterminate: true, hidden: !running, width: 24)
      ui.text(key: 'activity', content: activity[:text], wrap: false, ellipsize: :end, tooltip: tooltip,
              emphasis: running ? 'normal' : 'subtle')
      ui.button(key: 'stop', label: 'Stop', hidden: !running, tooltip: 'Stop what is queued or being cast (keeps the link)',
                on: { activate: window.cb { window.push([:stop]) } })
    end
  end

  # The right-click menu on a patient's figures. The browser opens it at
  # once, and reports which wound was under the pointer just before; the
  # chosen item takes that wound.
  def render_wound_menu(ui)
    window = self
    ui.group(key: 'wound-menu', menu: :context) do
      WOUND_METHODS.each do |label, method|
        ui.button(key: "wound-#{method}", label: label, on: { activate: window.cb { window.on_wound_menu(method) } })
      end
    end
  end

  # The tab header menus: right-click for link and take-all options,
  # double-click to close tabs. Each is opened by the script where the
  # pointer was, under a fresh key so it opens anew every time.
  def render_tab_menu(ui, data)
    menu = data[:tab_menu]
    return unless menu

    window = self
    name = menu[:name]
    ui.group(key: "tab-menu-#{data[:menu_revision]}", menu: :context, open: true, popup_position: menu[:at],
             on: { dismiss: window.cb { window.dismiss_tab_menu } }) do
      items = if menu[:kind] == :link
                [['Link Persistent', [:link, name, 'persistent']], ['Link Hodierna', [:link, name, 'hodierna']],
                 ['Link Unity', [:link, name, 'unity']], nil] +
                  [['Take All', nil], ['Take Part', 'part'], ['Take Half', 'half'], ['Take Most', 'most']].map do |label, method|
                    [label, [:link_take, name, method, :options]]
                  end
              else
                [['Close Tab', [:close_tab, name]], ['Close Other Tabs', [:close_others, name]]]
              end
      items.each_with_index do |(label, intent), index|
        next ui.divider(key: "tab-sep-#{index}") unless label

        ui.button(key: "tab-item-#{index}", label: label, on: { activate: window.cb { window.on_tab_menu(intent) } })
      end
    end
  end

  # ---- callbacks (WebUI host thread) ---------------------------------------

  def push(intent)
    @intents << intent
  end

  # Retouches the patient on the open tab. With no tab open it says how to add
  # one, on the status strip, rather than asking who. While a step is running
  # the strip is left alone, so its busy bar and Stop stay.
  def on_touch
    patient = selected_patient
    return push([:touch, patient]) if patient
    return if @lock.synchronize { @activity[:state] == :running }

    show_activity('TOUCH <name> or ;touch <name> adds a tab', nil, :done)
  end

  def on_break
    push([:break, selected_patient])
  end

  # A right-press on Break: stop and LINK ALL CANCEL.
  def on_break_press(payload)
    push([:break_all]) if payload[:button] == 3
  end

  def send_for_selected(kind)
    patient = selected_patient
    push([kind, patient, options]) if patient
  end

  def options
    @lock.synchronize { @options.dup }
  end

  def set_option(option, value)
    @lock.synchronize do
      @options[option] = value ? true : false
      @state = @state.merge('options' => @options.transform_keys(&:to_s))
    end
  end

  def set_click_amount(amount)
    @lock.synchronize do
      @options[:click_amount] = amount
      @state = @state.merge('options' => @options.transform_keys(&:to_s))
    end
  end

  def set_pinned(value)
    @lock.synchronize { @state = @state.merge('pinned' => value ? true : false) }
  end

  def reset_size
    @lock.synchronize do
      @resize_id += 1
      @size = [DEFAULT_WIDTH, DEFAULT_HEIGHT]
    end
    redefine
  end

  def on_select(payload)
    @lock.synchronize do
      name = @views.keys.find { |patient| self.class.key_for(patient) == payload[:tab] } || @views.keys[payload[:index].to_i]
      @selected = name if name
    end
    retitle
  end

  def on_tab_pointer(payload)
    name = @lock.synchronize { @views.keys.find { |patient| self.class.key_for(patient) == payload[:tab] } }
    return unless name

    kind = if payload[:button] == 3 && name != TouchParser::SELF
             :link
           elsif payload[:button] == 1 && payload[:click_count] == 2
             :close
           end
    return unless kind

    @lock.synchronize do
      @menu_revision += 1
      @tab_menu = { kind: kind, name: name, at: [payload[:x].to_i, payload[:y].to_i] }
    end
    refresh
  end

  def dismiss_tab_menu
    @lock.synchronize { @tab_menu = nil }
  end

  def on_tab_menu(intent)
    dismiss_tab_menu
    case intent.first
    when :close_tab then close_view(intent[1])
    when :close_others then (@lock.synchronize { @views.keys } - [intent[1]]).each { |other| close_view(other) }
    when :link_take then push(intent[0..2] + [options])
    else push(intent)
    end
  end

  # A left-click on a target.
  def on_region(name, region)
    target = self.class.target_for(region)
    return unless target && @lock.synchronize { @views.key?(name) }

    if target.first == :close
      close_view(name)
      return
    end
    flash(name, target)
    case target.first
    when :part then push([:take_wound, name, target[1], target[2], 'auto', options])
    else push([:take_condition, name, target.first.to_s, options])
    end
  end

  # Clicks on the figures outside a target are ignored; a right-click
  # remembers which wound the menu it opens is for.
  def on_surface(name, payload)
    return unless payload[:button] == 'secondary'

    target = self.class.target_for(payload[:region])
    @lock.synchronize do
      @right_target = target&.first == :part && name != TouchParser::SELF ? [name, target[1], target[2]] : nil
    end
  end

  def on_wound_menu(method)
    name, type, part = @lock.synchronize { @right_target }
    return show_activity('Right-click a wound to take part of it', nil, :done) unless name

    push([:take_wound, name, type, part, method, options])
  end

  # The browser reports the window's size and position as they change.
  def on_configure(payload)
    width = payload[:width].to_i
    height = payload[:height].to_i
    x, y = payload[:position]
    resized = false
    @lock.synchronize do
      if width >= MIN_WIDTH / 2 && height >= MIN_HEIGHT / 2
        resized = (width - @size[0]).abs > 4 || (height - @size[1]).abs > 4
        @size = [width, height]
        @state = @state.merge('width' => width, 'height' => height)
      end
      @state = @state.merge('x' => x, 'y' => y) if self.class.on_screen?(x, y, payload[:monitors])
    end
    refresh if resized
  end

  def on_close
    @closed = true
    push([:quit])
  end

  private

  def open_page
    window = self
    @page_events = { close: ->(_event) { window.on_close },
                     configure: window.cb(redraw: false) { |event| window.on_configure(event.payload) } }
    @page_props = { bare: true, viewport: true, min_width: MIN_WIDTH, min_height: MIN_HEIGHT }
    @page = Lich::API.webui_page(owner: @owner, id: PAGE_ID, title: 'Touch', props: @page_props, on: @page_events) do |ui|
      window.render(ui)
    end
    Lich::API.webui_refresh(@page)
    Lich::API.webui_start
    geometry = { width: @size[0], height: @size[1] }
    geometry[:position] = [@state['x'], @state['y']] if self.class.on_screen?(@state['x'], @state['y'])
    # The geometry saved in Vars, as the old window restored it.
    raise 'the window host refused to open it' unless Lich::WebUI.open(page: @page, geometry: geometry)
  end

  # Brings a tab forward. The tabs get a new key so every viewer shows the
  # chosen tab rather than keeping its own pick. Called under the lock.
  def select_tab(name)
    @selected = name
    @tabs_revision += 1
  end

  def close_view(name)
    @lock.synchronize do
      names = @views.keys
      index = names.index(name)
      return unless index

      @views.delete(name)
      if @selected == name || !@views.key?(@selected)
        remaining = @views.keys
        @selected = remaining[index] || remaining.last
      end
      @tabs_revision += 1
      @right_target = nil if @right_target&.first == name
    end
    push([:closed, name])
    retitle
  end

  # Briefly draws the clicked target pressed.
  def flash(name, target)
    @lock.synchronize do
      view = @views[name]
      return unless view

      view[:pressed] = target
    end
    refresh
    @scheduler ||= Lich::WebUI.callback_scheduler(owner: @owner)
    @scheduler.schedule(FLASH_MS) do
      @lock.synchronize { @views[name][:pressed] = nil if @views[name] }
      refresh
      false
    end
  rescue Lich::WebUI::Error
    nil
  end

  # The title names the patient on the tab being shown.
  def retitle
    redefine
  end

  def redefine
    title, props = @lock.synchronize do
      name = @selected if @views.key?(@selected)
      props = @page_props
      props = props.merge(resize_request: { id: "reset-#{@resize_id}", size: [DEFAULT_WIDTH, DEFAULT_HEIGHT] }) if @resize_id.positive?
      [name ? "Touch - #{name}" : 'Touch', props]
    end
    @page.refresh_definition(title: title, props: props, on: @page_events)
  end
end

class Touch
  HOOK_NAME = 'touch-window'.freeze
  STATE_KEY = 'touch_window'.freeze
  DEFAULT_OPTIONS = {
    'include_internal' => true,
    'include_scars'    => true,
    'quick'            => false,
    'half_on_major'    => false,
    'leave_bleeders'   => false,
    'click_amount'     => 'all'
  }.freeze
  # Built-in casting values. touch_self_spells only needs the spells and values
  # being changed, e.g. { 'hw' => { 'mana' => 10 } }; the rest come from here.
  # With no prep_time a spell is cast once the game says it is fully prepared.
  DEFAULT_SPELL = { 'mana' => 5 }.freeze
  # The longest to wait for full preparation before casting anyway.
  MAX_PREP_WAIT = 30
  NAME = /\A[A-Za-z][\w'-]*\z/
  PROMPT = %r{<prompt[^>]*>.*?</prompt>|<prompt[^>]*/>}
  # strip_xml buffer key, kept apart from Lich's own 'main' buffer.
  STRIP_TYPE = 'touch'.freeze
  DEBUG_TRIGGER = /empathic link|injuries include|Wounds to the/
  # Raw lines logged after each trigger in debug mode.
  DEBUG_LINES = 60

  # Keeps only the usable parts of touch_self_spells, so a missing, partial or
  # mistyped setting falls back to DEFAULT_SPELL instead of breaking a cast.
  #
  # @param custom [Object] the raw setting; nil when base.yaml predates it
  # @return [Hash{String => Hash}] abbreviation => the valid 'mana' / 'prep_time' overrides
  def self.spell_settings(custom)
    return {} unless custom.is_a?(Hash)

    custom.each_with_object({}) do |(abbrev, values), spells|
      next unless values.is_a?(Hash)

      values = values.transform_keys(&:to_s)
      tuned = {}
      tuned['mana'] = values['mana'] if values['mana'].is_a?(Integer) && values['mana'].positive?
      tuned['prep_time'] = values['prep_time'] if values['prep_time'].is_a?(Numeric) && !values['prep_time'].negative?
      spells[abbrev.to_s.downcase] = tuned
    end
  end

  def initialize(target)
    # The guild is nil until Lich has read INFO, so only a known non-empath is stopped.
    if DRStats.guild && !DRStats.empath?
      Lich::Messaging.msg('bold', "touch: only empaths can TOUCH to perceive wounds (Lich has you as #{DRStats.guild}).")
      exit
    end
    unless TouchWindow.available?
      Lich::Messaging.msg('bold', 'touch: this Lich cannot show WebUI windows (an older Lich, or one started with --no-gui), so the window cannot open.')
      exit
    end

    settings = get_settings
    @spells = self.class.spell_settings(settings.touch_self_spells)
    @parser = TouchParser.new(settings.touch_link_patterns)
    @patients = {}
    @lines = Thread::Queue.new
    @intents = Thread::Queue.new
    @pending = []
    @immediate = []
    @window = nil
    @debug = false

    before_dying { shutdown }
    install_hooks
    open_window
    @intents << [:touch, normalize(target)] if target
    run
  end

  private

  def install_hooks
    DownstreamHook.add(HOOK_NAME, proc { |server_string|
      @lines << server_string if server_string
      server_string
    })
    # A second ;touch would otherwise be refused as "already running".
    command = /\A(?:<c>)?#{$lich_char_regex || ';'}touch(?:\s+(?<target>[A-Za-z][\w'-]*))?\s*\z/i
    UpstreamHook.add(HOOK_NAME, proc { |client_string|
      match = command.match(client_string.to_s)
      next client_string unless match

      @intents << (match[:target] ? [:touch, normalize(match[:target])] : [:present])
      nil
    })
  end

  def open_window
    @window = TouchWindow.new(Script.current, @intents, load_state)
  rescue StandardError => e
    Lich::Messaging.msg('bold', "touch: could not open the window: #{e.message}")
    exit
  end

  def normalize(name)
    return :debug if name.to_s.casecmp?('debug')

    name.to_s.casecmp?('self') ? TouchParser::SELF : name.to_s.capitalize
  end

  def run
    loop do
      clear
      drain_lines
      break unless drain_intents

      send_immediate
      step = @pending.shift
      if step
        @interrupted = false
        @current = step
        show_status(step, :running)
        @busy = true
        perform(step[:action])
        @busy = false
        break if @quitting

        # The task's last step went out; the next task, if any, shows itself.
        show_status(step, :done) if step[:step] == step[:steps] && !@interrupted
      else
        pause(0.1)
      end
    end
  end

  # Shows a step on the window's status strip.
  #
  # @param state [Symbol] :running, :done or :stopped
  def show_status(step, state)
    text = TouchCommands.status_text(step, state)
    detail = TouchCommands.describe(step[:action])
    @window.show_activity(text, detail, state)
  end

  # Waits up to +seconds+, or until the block returns true, while still
  # reading the game and the window, so Break (or closing the window) can cut
  # a spell's preparation short.
  #
  # @return [Boolean] false if the wait was interrupted
  def wait_unless_stopped(seconds)
    deadline = Time.now + seconds
    while Time.now < deadline
      drain_lines
      @quitting = true unless drain_intents
      send_immediate unless @quitting
      return false if @interrupted || @quitting
      return true if block_given? && yield

      pause 0.1
    end
    true
  end

  # Game text arrives raw from the downstream hook, so the healing commands
  # this script sends with fput cannot swallow the lines the parser needs.
  def drain_lines
    changed = {}
    until @lines.empty?
      chunk = @lines.pop
      chunk.each_line do |raw|
        capture(raw) if @debug
        # A prompt ends the output before it, wherever it sits on the line.
        raw.split(PROMPT, -1).each_with_index do |piece, index|
          @parser.finish if index.positive?
          plain_lines(piece).each { |text| apply(@parser.feed(text), changed) }
        end
      end
    end
    publish(changed)
  end

  # Strips the XML the same way Lich does for every script's own game text, so
  # the parser sees what the player sees. The buffer key is touch's own, and a
  # stream split across lines comes back joined, possibly as several lines.
  #
  # @return [Array<String>] the non-blank lines of plain text in the piece
  def plain_lines(piece)
    text = strip_xml(piece, type: STRIP_TYPE)
    return [] unless text

    text.split(/\r?\n/).map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?)
  end

  # ;touch debug -- writes the raw XML around each TOUCH / PERCEIVE to a log
  # file, so unexpected game markup can be seen exactly as Lich received it.
  def capture(raw)
    @capture_left = DEBUG_LINES if DEBUG_TRIGGER.match?(raw)
    return unless @capture_left.to_i.positive?

    @capture_left -= 1
    File.open(@debug_log, 'a') { |file| file.puts(raw.inspect) }
  rescue StandardError => e
    @debug = false
    Lich::Messaging.msg('bold', "touch: debug log stopped: #{e.message}")
  end

  def start_debug
    @debug_log = File.join(defined?(LOG_DIR) ? LOG_DIR : Dir.pwd, 'touch-debug.log')
    @debug = true
    Lich::Messaging.msg('bold', "touch: logging raw TOUCH output to #{@debug_log}")
  end

  def apply(events, changed)
    events.each do |event|
      kind, name = event
      patient = (@patients[name] ||= TouchPatient.new(name))
      patient.apply(event)
      changed[name] ||= false
      changed[name] = true if kind == :patient
    end
  end

  # @param changed [Hash{String => Boolean}] patient name => whether to bring its tab forward
  def publish(changed)
    changed.each do |name, bring_forward|
      snapshot = @patients[name].snapshot
      bring_forward ? @window.show_patient(name, snapshot) : @window.update_patient(name, snapshot)
    end
  end

  # @return [Boolean] false once the window has been closed
  def drain_intents
    until @intents.empty?
      intent = @intents.pop
      return false if intent.first == :quit

      handle(intent)
    end
    true
  end

  def handle(intent)
    kind, patient, *details = intent
    label = TouchCommands.task_label(kind, patient, details)
    case kind
    when :touch
      if patient == :debug
        start_debug
      elsif patient == TouchParser::SELF || NAME.match?(patient.to_s)
        queue(TouchCommands.touch(patient), label, @immediate)
      end
    when :stop then stop
    when :break
      stop
      queue(TouchCommands.break_link(patient), label, @immediate)
    when :break_all
      stop
      queue([[:command, 'link all cancel']], label, @immediate)
    when :take_wound then queue(take_wound(patient, *details), label)
    when :take_condition then queue(TouchCommands.take_condition(patient, *details), label)
    when :take_all then queue(TouchCommands.take_all(patient, wounds_of(patient), details.first), label)
    when :take_minor then queue(TouchCommands.take_minor(patient, wounds_of(patient), details.first), label)
    when :link then queue(TouchCommands.link(patient, details.first), label)
    when :link_take then queue(TouchCommands.link_take(patient, *details), label)
    when :cast then queue([[:spell, details.first, nil]], label)
    when :present then @window.present
    when :closed then @patients.delete(patient)
    end
  end

  def take_wound(patient, type, part, method, options)
    return TouchCommands.take_wound(patient, type, part, method, quick: options[:quick]) unless method == 'auto'

    level = @patients[patient]&.level(type, part)
    unless level
      # Say why the click sent nothing, rather than leave it looking broken.
      where = TouchCommands.part_name(part)
      Lich::Messaging.msg('plain', "touch: #{patient} has no #{type.to_s.tr('_', ' ')} wound on the #{where} to take.")
      return []
    end

    TouchCommands.click_wound(patient, type, part, level, options)
  end

  def wounds_of(patient)
    @patients[patient]&.wound_list || []
  end

  # Each step remembers the task it belongs to and where it falls in it, for
  # the status strip ("Self: Heal all 2/9").
  #
  # @param into [Array] @pending, or @immediate for touches and breaks
  def queue(actions, label = nil, into = @pending)
    actions.each_with_index do |action, index|
      into << { action: action, label: label, step: index + 1, steps: actions.size }
    end
  end

  # Touches and breaks skip the queue. They go out at once, even while a spell
  # is being prepared or a take is running: a touch only refreshes what a tab
  # shows, and a break shouldn't wait behind the very thing it is stopping.
  # The status strip then goes back to the task in hand.
  def send_immediate
    return if @immediate.empty?

    until @immediate.empty?
      step = @immediate.shift
      show_status(step, :running)
      perform(step[:action])
      show_status(step, :done)
    end
    show_status(@current, :running) if @busy && !@interrupted
  end

  def perform(action)
    kind, *details = action
    case kind
    when :command
      waitrt?
      fput(details.first)
    when :spell
      cast_on_self(*details)
    end
  end

  # Break: drops everything queued and interrupts a spell being prepared.
  def stop
    stopped = @busy ? @current : @pending.first
    show_status(stopped, :stopped) if stopped
    @pending.clear
    @interrupted = true
  end

  def cast_on_self(abbrev, target)
    spell = DEFAULT_SPELL.merge(@spells.fetch(abbrev, {}))
    waitrt?
    return unless DRCA.prepare?(abbrev, spell['mana'])

    # Stopped mid-preparation: let the spell go rather than leave it held.
    return fput('release spell') unless wait_until_prepared(spell['prep_time'])

    DRCA.cast?(target ? "cast #{target}" : 'cast')
  end

  # Waits for a just-prepared spell to be ready to cast: a fixed number of
  # seconds when the spell has a prep_time, otherwise until the game's own
  # preparation timer runs out (it ends as "You feel fully prepared to cast
  # your spell." arrives), as DRCA does with waitcastrt?. The timer reaches
  # Lich with the prepare message; until it has been seen, a second is
  # allowed for it to land.
  #
  # @return [Boolean] false if Break or closing the window interrupted it
  def wait_until_prepared(prep_time)
    return wait_unless_stopped(prep_time) if prep_time

    started = Time.now
    timer_seen = false
    wait_unless_stopped(MAX_PREP_WAIT) do
      remaining = checkcastrt
      timer_seen ||= remaining.positive?
      (timer_seen || Time.now - started >= 1) && remaining <= 0
    end
  end

  def load_state
    saved = Vars[STATE_KEY]
    saved = {} unless saved.is_a?(Hash)
    options = DEFAULT_OPTIONS.merge(saved['options'].is_a?(Hash) ? saved['options'] : {})
    saved.merge('options' => options)
  end

  def shutdown
    return if @shut_down

    @shut_down = true
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK_NAME)
    UpstreamHook.remove(HOOK_NAME)
    window = @window
    return unless window

    Vars[STATE_KEY] = window.state
    window.destroy
  end
end

Touch.new(args.target)
